0.7.4
generated with tree-sitter-cli 0.26.12 (ABI 15)
local patches in grammar.js and src/scanner.c, on top of that commit:
- a custom operator is only the scanner token, so a `///**` comment after an expression stays a comment
- `await` of a property or prefix expression can leave the following brace to `if` / `while` / `for`
- `@available` may precede a freestanding macro such as `#Preview`
- `()` is an empty tuple
- a newline before `*` does not end the statement
- a `/` operator run yields to a regex when a later `/` on the line closes it, and `\/` is allowed in a regex body
- `/*` and `*/` inside a line string stay string text (`line_str_text` is scanned externally)
- a raw string may nest inside another raw string's interpolation
- `(T?, Array<U>).self` is a metatype of a tuple type
